   "a": "2Vm, 2f, and 2Vm per diode."
  },
  {
   "level": "remember",
   "q": "State the average output of a three-phase diode bridge in terms of the line RMS voltage.",
   "marks": 2,
   "a": "Vdc = (3√2/π) VL = 1.35 VL."
  },
  {
   "level": "understand",
   "q": "Why does the second capacitor of a half-wave doubler charge to 2Vm?",
   "marks": 3,
   "a": "On the negative half-cycle D1 charges C1 to Vm. On the positive half-cycle C1 is in series with the supply, so the voltage presented to D2 peaks at Vm (supply) + Vm (C1) = 2Vm, and C2 charges to that."
  },
  {
   "level": "apply",
   "q": "A three-phase diode bridge runs from 400 V, 50 Hz. Find Vdc, the lowest ripple frequency and the lowest output voltage in the ripple.",
   "marks": 4,
   "a": "VLm = 565.69 V; Vdc = 3 × 565.69/π = 540.2 V; ripple 6 × 50 = 300 Hz; lowest output VLm cos 30° = 489.9 V."
  },
  {
   "level": "apply",
   "q": "A half-wave doubler on a 230 V, 50 Hz supply uses C2 = 10 µF and supplies 2 mA. Estimate the no-load output and the ripple.",
   "marks": 4,
   "a": "2Vm = 2 × 325.27 = 650.5 V at no load. Ripple ≈ Idc/(fC2) = 0.002/(50 × 10 × 10⁻⁶) = 4.0 V peak to peak, at 50 Hz."
  },
  {
   "level": "analyze",
   "q": "A designer needs 600 V DC at 30 A from a 415 V three-phase supply. Compare a three-phase bridge with a single-phase bridge plus capacitor across two lines.",
   "marks": 6,
   "a": "Three-phase bridge: 1.35 × 415 = 560 V with 4.2 % ripple at 300 Hz and no capacitor, current shared by all three lines, PF about 0.955. A single-phase bridge with C across two lines draws all 30 A from two lines in narrow pulses, with 100 Hz ripple, poor PF and an unbalanced supply. The bridge wins; since 560 V is its maximum, 600 V needs a transformer tap of about 445 V."
  }
 ],
 "beyond": "Not for the exam. Large drives use 12-pulse and 18-pulse rectifiers: two or three bridges fed from phase-shifted transformer windings, so the 5th and 7th harmonics cancel. Kilovolt multipliers built from doubler stages power X-ray tubes and precipitators. Search for 'Cockcroft–Walton multiplier' and '12-pulse rectifier'.",
